orming the genus Anous, are a genus of seabirds in family Laridae which also contains the gulls, terns and skimmers. The genus contains five species.","revisionId":1350549409,"title":"Anous","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anous","wikidataId":"Q513741"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Javan Slow Loris","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Nycticebus javanicus","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Nycticebus javanicus É.Geoffroy Saint-Hilaire, 1812","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":5786064},"ottId":946857,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Nycticebus javanicus","synonyms":["Nycticebus coucang javanicus","Nycticebus ornatus"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The Javan slow loris (Nycticebus javanicus) is a strepsirrhine primate and a species of slow loris native to the western and central portions of the island of Java, in Indonesia. Although originally described as a separate species, it was considered a subspecies of the Sunda slow loris (N. coucang) for many years, until reassessments of its morphology and genetics in the 2000s resulted in its promotion to full species status.","revisionId":1356938611,"title":"Javan slow loris","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Javan_slow_loris","wikidataId":"Q972907"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Bolivian Squirrel Monkey","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"peruviensis","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Peruvian Squirrel Monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Black-capped Squirrel Monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Black-headed Squirrel Monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Bolivian/peruvian Squirrel Monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Saimiri boliviensis","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Saimiri boliviensis (I.Geoffroy Saint-Hilaire & de Blainville, 1834)","status":"ACCEPTED